.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt DISKCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm diskctl
.Nd reread a disk's partition table or print its identity
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm reread Ar DEVICE
.Nm
.Cm id Ar DEVICE
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command rereads a disk's partition table or prints its MBR signature.
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm reread Ar DEVICE
Issue
.Dv BLKRRPART
on the whole-disk node
.Ar DEVICE
to create nodes for partitions just written by a program.
The kernel refuses the request with
.Er EBUSY
while a file system on the disk is mounted or another descriptor is open
on the disk.
This prevents a reread from changing the partition bounds used by a
mounted file system.
.It Cm id Ar DEVICE
Print the disk's MBR signature as eight lowercase hexadecimal digits.
The signature is the four bytes at offset 440 in the first sector.
.Xr growroot 8
and the boot command line use it to identify the disk.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl diskctl id /dev/disk0
.Pp
The installer uses both commands.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
An invalid command or operand count prints:
.Dl usage: diskctl reread DEVICE | diskctl id DEVICE
Diagnostics identify the device.
A reread refused with
.Er EBUSY
prints:
.Dl diskctl: DEVICE is in use: unmount everything on it and close every program holding it
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr disk 7 ,
.Xr growroot 8
